41:| skylight | glass in the deck x6..9, z15..17, y=17 | | lights the top-floor room | roof part leaves it as an opening |
48:Material roles: BODY = painted horizontal siding (a mid sage/teal). TRIM = cream/white (cornices, window casings, columns, corner boards). ACCENT 1 = deep plum/maroon (brackets, sash frames, door, spandrel panels). ACCENT 2 = gold/ochre (fish-scale shingles, small dentils, pediment tympana). BASE = grey rusticated stone. Iron = black.
55:| 5..8 | storey 1 (parlour): bay windows; porch columns | see OPENINGS |
57:| 10..12 | storey 2: bay windows, a window pair over the porch | |
59:| 14..15 | storey 3: shorter bay windows, pair over the porch | |
65:Bay detailing: cream corner boards at every bay angle (x3,x6 at z=4; diagonals), y=4..16, flush or +1. Siding between windows in BODY. The diagonal wall cells carry their own single windows.
67:Porch: two cream COLUMNS at (10,5..8,7) and (14,5..8,7) with a base block at y=5 and a capital at y=8. Entablature y=9 z=6..7 x10..14 with a small gold pediment over the entry at x11..13 y=10, z=6 (+1, below the storey-2 window sill). Porch inner walls are BODY siding with a cream wainscot. The ceiling is plum-panelled.
71:Blank, full height y0..18, z7..30. Material: plain brick or stucco (a party wall, not painted siding) so the painted front reads as a mask, the SF look. The front cornice returns 1 cell onto each party wall at z=7..8, y=16..17. No openings.
74:BODY siding (same colour) over a stone base y0..3 (mostly buried: grade at y=2). Cream window casings, a simple 1-proud cream cornice at y=17 and the parapet at y=18. Window hoods are flat cream slabs (+1), with no pediments: the rear is for living, not show.
76:## OPENINGS
85:| N bay diagonals, S1 | single tall windows | 2 and 7 | 5..7 | 5 | 1 x 3 each |
86:| N bay diagonals, S1 | single tall windows | 1 and 8 | 5..7 | 6 | 1 x 3 each |
94:| S rear, S1 | windows | 3..4 and 11..12 | 6..7 | 30 | 2 x 2 each (over the counter) |
95:| S rear, S2 | windows | 3..4 and 11..12 | 10..12 | 30 | 2 x 3 each |
96:| S rear, S3 | windows | 3..4 and 11..12 | 14..15 | 30 | 2 x 2 each |
97:| S rear, garage level | small window above grade | 3..4 | 3 | 30 | 2 x 1 |
98:| roof | skylight | 6..9 | 17 | 15..17 | 4 x 3 |
100:Window ornament positions (later parts ADD these into air outside the wall, so nothing here is carved):
101:- Pediment hoods: plum/cream triangular hoods on stair blocks, one cell above each front window head (y=8, 13, 16), +1 proud (z=3 on the bay face, z=6 over the porch). On storey 3 the hood is a flat cream slab at y=16, between the brackets.
102:- Sills: cream slab +1 under each front window (y=4, 9, 13).
129:| 3 (top floor, under the roof) | 13 | 14 | 14..16 | 17 (roof deck) | TOP ROOM x1..12 z7..22 + bay (studio/den under the skylight z15..17), fireplace breast continues; box room x1..14 z23..29 |
150:| glass | glass_pane, glass (skylight) | white_stained_glass_pane for transoms |
160:## VOCABULARY
167:- **window(x0,x1,y0,y1,z,face)**: fill the opening with `glass_pane`; casing: `smooth_quartz` (x0-1 and x1+1, y0..y1, z-1 proud; skip where the neighbour is another window's casing or a corner board); `sill(x0..x1,y0-1,z-1)` = `smooth_quartz_slab type=top`; hood (see below). For rear windows: flat `smooth_quartz_slab type=bottom` hood at y1+1, z+1 (proud), no casing.
169:- **hoodSingle(x,y,z-1)**: single hood = one `smooth_quartz_slab type=bottom` one cell above the window head.
182:- **bayWall(storey y0..y1)**: face z=4 x3..6; diagonals (2,5),(7,5),(1,6),(8,6): `siding` from y0 to y1, spandrel and fishscale bands, window openings left air.
188:- **skylight**: opening x6..9 z15..17 y17: `glass`; curb `smooth_quartz_slab type=bottom` y18 around.
189:- **window ornaments summary** per plan FACADES: pediment hoods y8,13,16; sills y4,9,13.
221:1. **parts/shell.mjs, shell, floors, stairs-holes, partitions.** Ground base (grade y0 and y≤2 behind, sidewalk), party walls `bricks` x0/x15 z7..30 y0..18, front wall z=7 (`siding`, stone base y0..3) leaving porch x10..14 z7 y5..8 and window/door air, rear wall z=30 (stone y0..3, `siding` y4..17, parapet y18), slabs y0/4/9/13/17 with the three stair holes and skylight x6..9 z15..17, partitions per ROOMS, ceiling, every OPENING as air. Ticks 1,14,20,24.
223:3. **parts/roofs.mjs, roof deck & rooflines.** Deck y17 (`stone_slab`/gravel) with parapets y18 on party walls and rear, the front false-front parapet y18 + coping, `cornice` courses (main + bay ring + returns), `pediment`, `finial`, `chimney`, skylight curb, rear cornice. Ticks 9 (courses), 10, 18, 19.
224:4. **parts/openings.mjs, glazing & window dressing.** `window` (panes, casing, sill, hoods), `entryDoor`, `garageDoor`, rear French doors and windows, transoms, skylight glass. Ticks 2, 6, 8, 19, 20.
228:- [x] P1 shell  - [ ] P2 front  - [ ] P3 roofs  - [ ] P4 openings  - [ ] P5 ornament  - [ ] P6 site
231:- Never write into a reserved cell or into air a prior part left (runParts refuses). P1 leaves: openings, porch mouth, column cells, pilaster/cornice/bracket cells, stair holes, skylight.
235:- P1 (shell) notes: party walls are bricks y0..18 (the y18 parapet cells are brick already), so P3's side parapets and the chimney's x0 cells at y18 are refused as same-block writes. Partitions are `smooth_quartz` (white_terracotta is not on palette.json). Left to P2: porch floor y4 x10..14 z7..9 and porch side wall x9 z8..9 (P1 keeps those cells clear). Left to P4: entry casings at x10 and x13 y5..8 z10 (P1 keeps them air). Study doorway (11,10..11,10) is air. Ground partition at x=9 (laundry doorway (9,1..2,13)) is not built: plan gives no ground x=9 line. Floors use the ROOMS materials per box; deck is `gravel` y17 over x1..14 z8..29 with the skylight air. The make.sh roof preset then replaces the y17 deck (removes 420 blocks); that is the roof step's call, not P1's.
----
